When?

692
00:31:47,015 --> 00:31:48,600
Well, I've given my two weeks' notice,

693
00:31:48,900 --> 00:31:52,200 but I promise I'm gonna find you guys a great replacement before I go.

694
00:31:52,600 --> 00:31:54,885
Is this 'cause those
Carmel kids were so good?

695
00:31:54,915 --> 00:31:56,185
Because we can work harder.

696
00:31:56,215 --> 00:31:56,885
This isn't fair,

697
00:31:56,915 --> 00:31:57,985
Mr. Schuester.

698
00:31:58,015 --> 00:32:00,000
We can't do this without you.

699
00:32:00,500 --> 00:32:05,500
So does that mean that I don't have to be in the club anymore or...?

700
00:32:05,900 --> 00:32:07,700
This isn't about you guys.

701
00:32:08,300 --> 00:32:11,300
Being an adult is about having to make difficult choices.

702
00:32:12,400 --> 00:32:13,885
It's not like high school.

703
00:32:13,915 --> 00:32:17,800
Sometimes you have to give up the things that you love.

704
00:32:19,700 --> 00:32:22,300
One day you guys are going to grow up and understand that.

705
00:32:24,300 --> 00:32:28,000
I have... loved being your teacher.

706
00:32:50,300 --> 00:32:52,400
Need help grading those papers?

707
00:32:53,200 --> 00:32:55,585
It's actually an application for H.W. Menken.

708
00:32:55,615 --> 00:32:57,100
They're hiring.

709
00:32:58,000 --> 00:32:59,100
Come on.

710
00:32:59,300 --> 00:33:01,100
Accounting is sexy.

711
00:33:05,500 --> 00:33:07,100
I'll miss you.

712
00:33:07,600 --> 00:33:09,985
Before you leave, can you do me a favor?

713
00:33:10,015 --> 00:33:10,285
Yeah.

714
00:33:10,315 --> 00:33:14,600
I made an appointment for you tomorrow in the career center.

715
00:33:15,100 --> 00:33:16,185
You need some guidance.

716
00:33:16,215 --> 00:33:18,000
I'm having a kid, Emma.

717
00:33:18,500 --> 00:33:20,185
What I need is better benefits.

718
00:33:20,215 --> 00:33:23,500
Just come, Will, for me.

719
00:33:30,600 --> 00:33:32,085
Didn't see you at
Glee Club today.

720
00:33:32,115 --> 00:33:33,785
Is that still happening?

721
00:33:33,815 --> 00:33:35,100
I've taken over.

722
00:33:35,600 --> 00:33:36,485
I'm interim director,

723
00:33:36,515 --> 00:33:38,585 but I expect the position will become permanent.

724
00:33:38,615 --> 00:33:40,685
- Hi, Finn, RuPaul.
- Hey.

725
00:33:40,715 --> 00:33:42,500
What are you doing talking to her?

726
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:45,900
Science project -- we're partners.

727
00:33:47,500 --> 00:33:49,685
Christ Crusaders tonight at 5:00, my house.

728
00:33:49,715 --> 00:33:51,200
Sounds great.

729
00:33:53,800 --> 00:33:55,400
Look, I - I should go.

730
00:33:55,800 --> 00:33:56,885
I can't do Glee anymore.

731
00:33:56,915 --> 00:33:57,885
It conflicts with...

732
00:33:57,915 --> 00:33:59,400
Your reputation?

733
00:34:00,200 --> 00:34:02,785
You've really got something, Finn, and you're throwing it away.

734
00:34:02,815 --> 00:34:06,500
- I... I'm gonna be late.
- You can't keep worrying about what people think of it.

735
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:09,500
You're better than all of them.

736
00:34:15,400 --> 00:34:17,600
What do you want me to do, apologize?

737
00:34:18,300 --> 00:34:19,900
That's not me, dude.

738
00:34:22,100 --> 00:34:25,900
Look, if I joined the flag team, you'd beat the crap outta me.

739
00:34:26,300 --> 00:34:27,685
I just don't understand why you did it.

740
00:34:27,715 --> 00:34:31,385
Schuester told me he'd give me enough extra credit to pass Spanish if 
I joined the club.

741
00:34:31,415 --> 00:34:32,985
I... I didn't have a choice.

742
00:34:33,015 --> 00:34:35,385
If I failed another class,
I'd be off the team.

743
00:34:35,415 --> 00:34:37,985
Look, it's over, okay, I quit.

744
00:34:38,015 --> 00:34:39,185
Anything else?

745
00:34:39,215 --> 00:34:40,700
No, that's it.

746
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:43,985
And as a welcome back to the world of the normal...

747
00:34:44,015 --> 00:34:45,800
I got you a present.

748
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:49,400
What's that noise?

749
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:51,585
Oh, God.

750
00:34:51,615 --> 00:34:53,185
Help, help!

751
00:34:53,215 --> 00:34:55,385
- Help!
- Is someone in there?

752
00:34:55,415 --> 00:34:57,485
We got that wheelchair kid inside.

753
00:34:57,515 --> 00:34:59,085
We're going to flip it.

754
00:34:59,115 --> 00:35:00,585
Isn't that kind of dangerous?

755
00:35:00,615 --> 00:35:02,185
He's already in a wheelchair.

756
00:35:02,215 --> 00:35:04,400
Come on, dude, we saved you the first roll.

757
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:13,200
Thank you.
Thank you so much.

758
00:35:13,900 --> 00:35:14,985
Thank you.

759
00:35:15,015 --> 00:35:17,885
- Oh, my God, the smell.
- What the hell, dude?

760
00:35:17,915 --> 00:35:19,685
I can't believe you're helping out this loser.

761
00:35:19,715 --> 00:35:21,300
Don't you get it, man?

762
00:35:21,600 --> 00:35:23,485
We're all losers --

763
00:35:23,515 --> 00:35:25,500 everyone in this school.

764
00:35:25,900 --> 00:35:27,985
Hell, everyone in this town.

765
00:35:28,015 --> 00:35:32,585
Out of all the kids who graduate, maybe half will go to college a-and two...

766
00:35:32,615 --> 00:35:34,400 will leave the state to do it.

767
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:36,285
I'm not afraid of being called a loser

768
00:35:36,315 --> 00:35:38,900
'cause I can accept that that's what I am.

769
00:35:39,400 --> 00:35:42,285
But I am afraid of turning my back on something that actually  made me happy 

770
00:35:42,315 --> 00:35:44,585 for the first time in my sorry life.

771
00:35:44,615 --> 00:35:46,185
So what?

772
00:35:46,215 --> 00:35:48,185
Are you quitting to join Homo Explosion?

773
00:35:48,215 --> 00:35:49,485
No.

774
00:35:49,515 --> 00:35:51,285
I'm doing both.

775
00:35:51,315 --> 00:35:53,900
'Cause you can't win without me and neither can they.

776
