♪ Hidin' ♪

782
00:36:18,515 --> 00:36:24,700
♪ Somewhere in the night... ♪

783
00:36:26,600 --> 00:36:28,485
Look, you guys, these steps are not hard.

784
00:36:28,515 --> 00:36:30,385
I've been doing them since preschool.

785
00:36:30,415 --> 00:36:32,085
I'm sorry, did I miss the election for queen?

786
00:36:32,115 --> 00:36:33,185
Because I didn't vote for you.

787
00:36:33,215 --> 00:36:34,385
I know what I'm talking about.

788
00:36:34,415 --> 00:36:37,885
I won my first dance competition when I was three months old.

789
00:36:37,915 --> 00:36:39,385
This is a closed rehearsal.

790
00:36:39,415 --> 00:36:43,300
Look, I owe you guys an apology.

791
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:45,700
I never should have quit.

792
00:36:47,100 --> 00:36:49,985
I don't want to be the guy that just drives around throwing eggs at people.

793
00:36:50,015 --> 00:36:50,785
That was you?

794
00:36:50,815 --> 00:36:52,885
You and your friends threw pee balloons at me.

795
00:36:52,915 --> 00:36:55,085
I know. You nailed all my lawn furniture to my roof.

796
00:36:55,115 --> 00:36:58,385
I wasn't actually there for that, but I'm really sorry.

797
00:36:58,415 --> 00:37:02,085
Look, that isn't who I am, and I'm tired of it.

798
00:37:02,115 --> 00:37:05,000
This is what I want to be doing, with you guys.

799
00:37:05,600 --> 00:37:06,885
I used to think that this was, like,

800
00:37:06,915 --> 00:37:10,585 the lamest thing on Earth, and maybe it is, but...

801
00:37:10,615 --> 00:37:12,500 we're all here for the same reason --

802
00:37:13,600 --> 00:37:15,600
'cause we want to be good at something.

803
00:37:17,300 --> 00:37:19,585
Arty, you play guitar, right?

804
00:37:19,615 --> 00:37:21,485
Think you could recruit the jazz band?

805
00:37:21,515 --> 00:37:22,685
I do have pull there.

806
00:37:22,715 --> 00:37:24,185
All right.

807
00:37:24,215 --> 00:37:25,185
Mercedes,

808
00:37:25,215 --> 00:37:27,285 we need new costumes, a-and they have to be cool.

809
00:37:27,315 --> 00:37:28,485
- Can you do that?
- Damn,

810
00:37:28,515 --> 00:37:30,300 don't you see what I got on?

811
00:37:30,600 --> 00:37:33,600
Rachel, you can do choreography.

812
00:37:34,400 --> 00:37:37,485
- Tina, what are you good at?
- I-I...

813
00:37:37,515 --> 00:37:39,285
We'll figure something out for you. And...

814
00:37:39,315 --> 00:37:42,000 what are you bringing to the table, Justin Timberlake?

815
00:37:43,500 --> 00:37:45,100
I got the music.

816
00:37:50,100 --> 00:37:52,100
I want to show you something.

817
00:37:54,900 --> 00:37:57,000
I did a little research...

818
00:37:58,400 --> 00:38:02,800 and this is a tape I found in the library of the '93 team at nationals.

819
00:38:04,500 --> 00:38:05,985
♪ Let's dance! ♪

820
00:38:06,015 --> 00:38:09,100
("That's The Way (I Like It)" playing)

821
00:38:11,900 --> 00:38:13,900
Do you know who that is?

822
00:38:16,200 --> 00:38:17,385
That's you, Will.

823
00:38:17,415 --> 00:38:18,985
♪ I like it, uh-huh, uh-huh ♪

824
00:38:19,015 --> 00:38:20,385
♪ When you take me... ♪

825
00:38:20,415 --> 00:38:22,900
That's you happier than I've ever seen you.

826
00:38:24,600 --> 00:38:27,000
That was the greatest moment of my life.

827
00:38:27,900 --> 00:38:29,085
Why?

828
00:38:29,115 --> 00:38:31,400
Because I loved what I was doing.

829
00:38:32,900 --> 00:38:36,100
I knew before we were halfway through with that number that we were going to win.

830
00:38:41,100 --> 00:38:45,000
Being a part of that, in that moment...

831
00:38:47,700 --> 00:38:50,000
...I knew who I was in the world.

832
00:38:58,400 --> 00:39:00,985
And the only time I've felt...
I've felt that way since then was...

833
00:39:01,015 --> 00:39:05,100 was when Terri told me
I was going to be a father.

834
00:39:08,600 --> 00:39:09,585
No.

835
00:39:09,615 --> 00:39:12,000
No, I need to provide for my family.

836
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:14,685
But provide what exactly?

837
00:39:14,715 --> 00:39:17,885
The understanding that money is the most important thing

838
00:39:17,915 --> 00:39:25,300 or the idea that the only life worth living is one that you're really passionate about Will.

